      "content": "In phonetics, voiced and unvoiced alveolar fricatives are distinguished by the degree of vocal cord vibration. The voiceless /s/ sound, also known as the \" Releases-only\" s, is produced when the vocal cords are completely relaxed or not vibrating at all, while the voiced /z/ sound is made by the vocal cords vibrating positively. As a result, the air flow over the alveolar ridge is less turbulent in the /s/ case, and more in the /z/ case.",
